    "help": {
        "title": "WarpScout Guide",
        "step1Title": "1. Basic Scanning",
        "step1Text": "Select the <b>AmneziaWG</b> protocol and the <b>Standard</b> preset. Click \"Scan\". The program will find endpoints that allow traffic through your ISP.",
        
        "step2Title": "2. Telegram Check",
        "step2Text": "If you need Telegram access, check the <b>\"Check Telegram\"</b> box. The program will send test MTProto requests to all 5 Telegram data centers.",
        "step2Item1": "<span style=\"color: #4caf50; font-weight: bold;\">ok</span> — all data centers are reachable. The ping to the slowest one is shown in parentheses.",
        "step2Item2": "<span style=\"color: #ff9800; font-weight: bold;\">3/5</span> or <span style=\"color: #ff9800; font-weight: bold;\">1/5</span> — only some data centers are reachable. Some Telegram accounts might not connect.",
        "step2Item3": "<span style=\"color: #f44336; font-weight: bold;\">blocked</span> — Telegram is completely blocked on this endpoint.",
        "step2Outro": "The <b>\"Telegram Only\"</b> checkbox hides all endpoints where the status is not <i>ok</i>.",
        
        "step3Title": "3. Auto I1 Selection (AmneziaWG)",
        "step3Text": "If you haven't specified a custom I1 in the advanced settings, the scanner will automatically test 5 built-in profiles (starting with QUIC). The current attempt (e.g., <code>I1 1/5</code>) will be shown in the bottom bar. The scanner will stop once it finds enough working tunnels.",
        
        "step4Title": "4. Node Filtering",
        "step4Text": "The table has a NODE column (data center code). Russian nodes (e.g., <code>DME</code>) are often blocked for Telegram and some services. To exclude them:",
        "step4Item1": "<b>\"Exclude countries\"</b> field → <code>RU</code>",
        "step4Item2": "<b>\"Exclude nodes\"</b> field → <code>DME</code>",
        
        "step5Title": "5. Saving Config",
        "step5Text": "Click on the best endpoint (with TG <i>ok</i> and low ping) and click <b>\"Save Selected\"</b>. Or click <b>\"Save Best\"</b> to let the program choose the fastest one.",
        
        "tipsTitle": "Useful Tips",
        "tip1": "If standard ports are blocked, use \"Port Sweep\" in the advanced panel.",
        "tip2": "If AmneziaWG doesn't work, try MASQUE (TCP) — it often works where AWG is blocked.",
        "tip3": "If nothing is found, run \"Find AWG junk\" in the \"Tools\" tab."
    },
